; A TYPENAME as a range bound (`uint..10`) aborts: the range arm reads both bounds as literal
; values and panics on anything else, before the head name is resolved at all. Name-INDEPENDENT —
; the same abort fires for every head, supported names included — so it is a defect on the SHAPE
; axis, not on the refused-name one; it is the recorded reason the refused-name closure sweep
; (`refused_name_closure_tests`) excludes this column instead of sweeping it, and that exclusion
; goes stale loudly when this row flips.
x = uint..10
